35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, wow! The evening groups survived without help, but the digitisation project stalled. That’s a huge difference!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, precisely. The digitisation project is a cautionary tale. We must avoid repeating that error. I’ll examine the running and equipment lines to see where the strain lies.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, the ledger confirms my suspicion. The vehicle line overran by a third, yet equipment was underutilized. We are bleeding cash on logistics, not skills.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, the vehicle overrun is a symptom. The grant pays only twelve months, then the flat budget absorbs the cost. That structural gap is the real danger.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, that gap is scary. But my data shows the outer wards lost their bus link. An hour’s trip is a wall no grant can fix.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that’s heartbreaking! But my volunteer data shows we have skilled retirees ready to help. Maybe we can bring the service to them?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, bringing service to them is wise, but only if the logistics don’t collapse. I’ll check the quoted delivery windows to see if suppliers can actually reach those outer wards.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, delivery windows are irrelevant if the staff cannot supervise the new facilitators. The roster lacks the necessary oversight skills.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, oversight is vital, but the grant’s twelve-month limit means we cannot sustain new roles. We must choose a service that fits the flat budget, not one that demands extra supervision.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, I agree. The flat budget is a hard limit. But if the bus is gone, no service reaches them. We must plan for the hour’s trip.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, I hear you. But my data shows the evening groups thrive without extra staff! We should pick something that runs itself, like those groups.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, self-sustaining is the only model that survives the grant’s expiration. I’ll verify the evening room bookings to see if that demand is real or just nostalgia.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, demand is irrelevant if the roster cannot execute it. I will examine the evening room bookings to verify if the existing staff can actually manage the load.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, demand is real, but the flat budget is the true constraint. We must select a service that requires no new recurring costs after the grant expires.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, I agree. But if the roads close, even a self-sustaining service is unreachable. We must account for the winter isolation.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, winter is tough, but the evening groups prove we can adapt! Let’s pick a service that works even when the roads close.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Daisuke, winter isolation is a constraint, not a reason to abandon the outer wards. I’ll examine the remote catalogue use to see if digital access bridges that physical gap.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, digital access is a workaround, not a solution. It ignores the physical strain on our already stretched staff. I will examine the evening room bookings to verify the actual load.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, digital access is a stopgap. The flat budget is the hard wall. We must choose a service that generates no new recurring costs after the grant expires.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, digital access helps, but it doesn't replace the physical barrier. I’ll stick with my findings on the bus links and winter closures to see who is truly cut off.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
