61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, Option C mirrors the partner-run groups that survived. But I need to verify if the facilitators are actually trained. I’ll check the volunteer register.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, the register is a list, not a guarantee. Option C demands trained facilitators we do not possess. We cannot assume skills exist.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, the register is a list, not a guarantee. Option C demands recurring facilitator fees. The grant expires, and the flat budget cannot absorb that new line.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, I agree. But Option D is the only one that reaches the outer wards. The bus is gone, so we must go to them.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, I hear you! But Option D needs a vehicle and staff. My data shows we lack supervisors. Option C uses partners who are already there!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Daisuke, Option D repeats the vehicle overrun Shion found. We cannot afford a new logistics line. Option C’s partner model is the only one that survived the last cycle.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, precisely. Option D demands a driver and a supervisor. The roster has neither. We would be hiring for a role that does not exist.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, precisely. Option D’s vehicle line already overran by a third. The flat budget cannot absorb that recurring strain. Option C’s partner model avoids new recurring costs entirely.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, I hear the cost worry. But the bus is gone. Option D is the only way to reach the outer wards before winter cuts them off.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, I understand the urgency! But Option C’s partners are already in the outer wards. They don’t need a bus; they just need a room.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Daisuke, the attendance sheets prove the outer wards demand service, but Option D’s vehicle costs are a trap. Option C’s partner model is the only one that survived without new recurring costs.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, the vehicle is a trap. Option C relies on partners, but the roster lacks supervisors to manage them. We cannot assume oversight exists.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, the vehicle is a trap. Option C’s partner model avoids new recurring costs. The flat budget cannot absorb the vehicle strain. We must choose sustainability over reach.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Yumi, I hear you. But a room in the main branch is still an hour away. Option C doesn't fix the physical wall I found.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, you’re right, the distance is real. But Option C’s partners are already there! They bridge the gap without us needing a bus. Let’s trust the community!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Daisuke, the partners are already in the outer wards. Option C bridges the gap without the vehicle trap. I vote for C.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, I concur. Option C is the only model that does not demand skills we lack. The partners provide the oversight. I vote for C.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, precisely. Option C’s partner model avoids the vehicle trap and new recurring costs. The flat budget can sustain it. I vote for C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, I see the partners are already there. Option C reaches them without the vehicle trap. I vote for C.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
